<p>These Rider Terms apply to riders, passengers and people booking transportation provided or arranged by Koast. The terms accepted for each ride determine its cancellation policy, included services and pricing rules. Driver app access and operator software use have their own <a href="/terms/driver/">Driver App Terms</a> and <a href="/terms/connect/">Connect Terms</a>. All roles are covered by the shared <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
<p>If you separately accept a <a href="/terms/standing-authorization/">Standing Booking and Payment Authorization</a>, it can cover requested bookings and saved-method payments within the identified company, account, service scope, limits and agreed pricing/ride-policy framework. These Rider Terms, signing in or an already saved card do not by themselves establish that authorization. The applicable reservation still needs the Company's acceptance and booking confirmation.</p>
<h2 id="general-provisions">1. General provisions</h2>
  <p>Koast is operated by Krujim Inc, headquartered in San Francisco, California. Koast provides chauffeured transportation directly and also arranges transportation with independent Transportation Service Providers ("TSPs"), depending on the reservation. Users may book through Koast's online platform, integrated third-party platforms, mobile applications or directly with Koast (collectively, the "Koast Tools").</p>
  <p>These General Terms and Conditions ("T&amp;Cs") apply to bookings for transportation provided directly by Krujim Inc and transportation arranged by Koast with an independent TSP. References to the TSP in the service provisions mean the operator providing the ride, including Krujim Inc for directly operated rides, as applicable.</p>
  <p id="ride-specific-terms"><strong>Terms for your ride.</strong> The quote, booking details and policies disclosed for a ride and accepted when it is booked form part of your agreement. For cancellation, refunds, no-shows, included time and mileage, waiting and other service charges, those accepted ride-specific terms take precedence over general descriptions on this website. Each leg of a reservation may have different terms, which must be identified for that leg. Later changes to a website, price list or operator policy do not retroactively change an accepted ride. Any agreed change to your booking must identify the revised service, price and affected terms. Mandatory rights under applicable law continue to apply.</p>

  <h2 id="booking-confirmation">2. Contractual relationship and contract conclusion</h2>
  <p><strong>2.1 Contractual relationship.</strong> For rides operated directly by Krujim Inc, Koast is the transportation service provider. For rides fulfilled by an independent TSP, Koast arranges the transportation and the independent TSP provides the ride. Contact Koast if you need to confirm which operator will fulfill your reservation.</p>
  <p><strong>2.2 Booking confirmation.</strong> A quote or acknowledgment of a ride request does not by itself confirm a reservation. A booking is confirmed when Koast accepts it and provides a booking confirmation through the app, email or another agreed booking channel. Review the confirmed itinerary, responsible operator, price and ride-specific terms. If a material detail is incorrect or a policy is missing or unclear, contact the booking provider promptly for clarification. A missing policy must not be replaced with an assumed fee or a later version of the operator's rules.</p>

  <h2 id="registration">3. Registration obligation</h2>
  <p>The user provides assurance to Koast that all information it transmits or has transmitted to Koast on its behalf by another person is complete and accurate. Registrations by automated processes are prohibited.</p>

  <h2 id="transportation">4. Selected content of the transportation contract</h2>
  <p><strong>4.1 Ride types, service changes.</strong> Depending on local availability, the user can select ride requests that include transfer rides, long-distance rides (transfer rides starting at 100 miles), rides on demand ("chauffeur hailing") and hourly bookings. If the ride actually carried out involves additional expenditure of effort due to requests that differ from the initially requested ride, the TSP will accommodate these requests to the extent possible; additional effort may result in additional costs (see Section 5). Subject to availability, changes may be requested even after conclusion of the contract but may result in additional charges.</p>
  <p>For transfers and long-distance rides, the agreed price covers the itinerary and inclusions stated for the ride. For hourly service, the accepted ride terms identify the minimum duration, included distance, billing start and end points, time precision and any additional time or mileage rates. Some rides may use garage departure and return rather than passenger pickup and dropoff as the billing basis; that basis must be disclosed and accepted for the ride. These general terms do not impose a universal pickup-only clock or half-hour rounding rule.</p>
  <p><strong>4.2 Pickup time.</strong> The booking confirmation identifies the pickup schedule and any agreed flight-based adjustment. Provide the correct flight number, airport and travel date, and tell the booking provider about changes. Flight tracking can help coordinate pickup; the ride-specific terms determine how arrival changes affect pickup, the waiting clock and included time.</p>
  <p><strong>4.3 Vehicle class, upgrades.</strong> Depending on regional availability, the user can choose from different vehicle classes (for example "Business Class Sedan", "Business Class SUV", "First Class Sedan", "First Class SUV", or "Sprinter Class"). Vehicles shown in the Koast Tools are illustrative examples; there is no right to a particular vehicle model within a booked class. Koast may upgrade a booking to a higher vehicle class at any time at no additional cost, depending on availability: "Business Class Sedan" may be upgraded to "Business Class SUV", "First Class SUV", or "First Class Sedan"; "Business Class SUV" may be upgraded to "First Class SUV". Koast will never downgrade your vehicle to a cheaper vehicle type or a smaller one — for example, sending a Sedan if you reserved an SUV.</p>
  <p><strong>4.4 Transport safety.</strong> The price in the booking confirmation includes the number of pieces of luggage specified in the booking form. Excess or bulky luggage (such as a wheelchair), weapons, or animals must be specified during booking; the TSP may refuse transport of items not agreed upon, including animals not housed in a closed, suitable transport box, except where local law requires accommodation. If the TSP permits carriage of additional items, surcharges may apply. The need for child restraints must be specified in the ride request, including the number and age of children and the type of restraints required. The transport of unaccompanied minors may be rejected by the TSP. The maximum number of passengers and luggage for a specific vehicle is set out in a binding luggage policy; the TSP may refuse transport where space and safety conditions do not permit it. If transport is refused because mandatory requirements were not correctly communicated by the user, Koast remains entitled to compensation.</p>
  <p><strong>4.5 Delays.</strong> Exceptional situations such as air traffic control strikes or inclement weather can only be compensated to a limited extent; in these cases longer waiting times or short-notice cancellations must be accepted.</p>
  <h3 id="cancellations">4.6 Cancellations, rebookings and no-shows</h3>
  <p>Cancellation deadlines, applicable charges, refundable amounts and no-show conditions depend on the terms disclosed for the particular ride and accepted when it was booked. They may vary by operator, service, vehicle class, date and reservation leg. These general terms do not create a universal cancellation window, refund percentage or no-show charge.</p>
  <p>Cancel through the cancellation control in the app where available, or contact the booking provider through the support channels identified in your confirmation. For Koast bookings, you may also contact Koast directly. Email is not the only accepted cancellation method. Keep the cancellation confirmation or record of your request. The applicable deadline is assessed against the time a valid cancellation is received through an accepted channel, rather than a later support reply. If an app request fails or its result is uncertain, contact the booking provider promptly.</p>
  <p>A request to change or rebook a ride is not automatically a cancellation. The booking provider must explain any effect on the original reservation, any charge under its accepted terms, and the revised ride terms before you agree to the change. No-show decisions must follow the accepted ride's conditions, including its applicable pickup or flight-based clock, waiting allowance and contact requirements. Missing or unclear accepted terms require review; a current policy or default penalty must not be substituted after the fact.</p>
  <p><strong>4.7 Behavior in the vehicle.</strong> During the entire ride, applicable road traffic rules apply to all guests, particularly seat belt requirements. The TSP's instructions must be followed. Guests may not open doors during the ride, throw objects from the vehicle, extend any body part from or scream from the vehicle. Use of equipment in the vehicle requires the TSP's prior permission. Smoking is prohibited; violations bear the cost of vehicle cleaning and resulting loss of serviceability. Food is discouraged; alcoholic drinks only with prior consent.</p>

  <h2 id="pricing-payment">5. Remuneration and payment</h2>
  <p><strong>5.1 Agreed price and inclusions.</strong> The accepted booking details identify the price, itinerary and included services. Required fees must be included in the displayed price as required by applicable law. Any permitted separately stated government charges must be disclosed. Optional extras, conditional service charges and their calculation basis must be explained before you agree to them. A general rate list published or changed after booking does not reprice an accepted ride.</p>
  <p><strong>5.2 Ride changes and additional service.</strong> Additional stops, a changed itinerary, extended time, excess mileage or other requested services may affect the price under the ride's accepted terms or a revised quote you agree to. The accepted terms determine any minimum duration, billing precision, additional rates and treatment of an early finish. A later change to an operator's pricing settings is not authorization to charge a different rate for your ride.</p>
  <p><strong>5.3 Waiting, hourly time and mileage.</strong> The ride-specific terms identify any included waiting allowance, when its clock starts, how flight changes are handled, and the rate and billing precision for chargeable waiting. They also identify included hourly time and mileage, any garage-based travel, and additional time or mileage charges. These allowances and rates may differ by ride; there is no universal waiting allowance or mileage schedule in these general terms. Time already included in hourly service must not also be billed as separate waiting. Any additional charge must be supported by the accepted terms and the service actually provided.</p>
  <p><strong>5.4 Payment.</strong> Accepted payment methods, any deposit, payment authorization and due dates are stated for your booking or agreed billing arrangement. Charges, refunds and credits must follow the accepted ride terms and actual payment records. These general terms do not authorize an undisclosed reminder or processing fee. Contact the booking provider if an amount or payment outcome is unclear. Vouchers are subject to the conditions disclosed when issued and cannot be redeemed for cash unless required by law.</p>

